---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/compare/recart-vs-postscript';
const title = 'Recart vs Postscript for Shopify SMS: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Recart is not simply a cart-only alternative. Compare how each platform acquires subscribers, supports your operator and executes campaigns alongside recovery.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "How should a Shopify team choose between Recart and Postscript?",
    "answer": "Compare acquisition, launch execution, cart cancellation and service scope. Both have broader SMS roles than cart-only versus broadcast-only."
  },
  {
    "question": "How does pricing compare?",
    "answer": "Obtain quotes for the same send plan and service requirements, including usage, carrier fees, minimums and any variable charges."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which has better abandoned cart SMS?",
    "answer": "Use the purchase-cancellation and inventory-change exercise. This comparison has no observed recovery-rate result."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I migrate between them?",
    "answer": "Plan permission and suppression transfer, number requirements and flow cutover. Establish readiness before selecting dates; no universal migration duration is promised."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I also consider Sequenzy?",
    "answer": "Consider it for an identified email requirement and verify its commerce event mapping. It does not automatically coordinate suppression with either SMS sender."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Postscript broadcast SMS matter versus Recart?",
    "answer": "Campaign execution matters, but Recart also advertises campaigns and automation. Compare the release approval and correction workflow in both."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should legacy Facebook Messenger decide this comparison?",
    "answer": "Only if you have a current supported Messenger requirement. Obtain explicit present-day support confirmation rather than choosing from historical positioning."
  },
  {
    "question": "What workflow test should decide the choice?",
    "answer": "Run the proposed footwear release and cart collision exercises, recording approvals, correction effort and permission handling."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-cyan-100/90">/</span>
        <span class="text-cyan-100/90">Recart vs Postscript</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="badge">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Recart vs Postscript for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Recart is not simply a cart-only alternative. Compare how each platform acquires subscribers, supports your operator and executes campaigns alongside recovery.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Comparing SMS acquisition, service and launch operations</h2>
        <p>Scope checked on November 24, 2026. This is a source-based comparison and proposed evaluation plan; no account tests or merchant results are claimed.</p>
        <h2>Current scope</h2>
        <p>Recart advertises OneClick opt-in, list growth, campaigns, cart and browse recovery, automation and client strategy. Postscript lists acquisition tools, automations and response management; its pricing page also describes a managed service. Neither should be reduced to a cart-versus-broadcast category.</p>
        <h2>Proposed exercise: footwear release with a late inventory change</h2>
        <p>Draft a release campaign for an opted-in audience. Before approval, remove an unavailable size and change the landing collection. Ask each team to show how the audience, message and links are corrected, who approves the change and how a queued send is stopped. This tests launch execution rather than claiming either vendor generated a past sales result.</p>
        <h2>Compare OneClick and the full permission record</h2>
        <p>Evaluate Recart OneClick alongside the Postscript signup method available to your store. Test a new visitor, an existing subscriber and a shopper who previously opted out. Inspect the saved source and permission state, confirmation experience and duplicate handling. Compare completed permitted subscriptions and the shopping experience, not a vendor headline conversion multiple.</p>
        <h2>Cart recovery and campaign collisions</h2>
        <p>Propose a cart flow for the same launch. Have a test shopper place an order after entering the flow but before the delayed message. The pending promotion should follow your documented cancellation rule. Also inspect whether an inventory change updates the product link and whether the cart flow collides with the release campaign. Agree a channel priority rule with your email owner.</p>
        <h2>Service is a deliverable, not a label</h2>
        <p>Request a written allocation of strategy, copy, design, scheduling, approval and reply monitoring. Ask what happens when a campaign needs an urgent correction outside the normal support window. Recart client strategy and Postscript managed services are relevant, but public descriptions do not establish the exact work or response commitment included in your quote.</p>
        <h2>Compare costs without attribution double counting</h2>
        <p>Use one send calendar and recipient distribution for both quotes. Separate base fees, usage, carrier charges, service and any minimum commitment. Hypothetical contribution example: $800 of incremental gross margin less $240 of messaging and $160 of extra labor leaves $400 before other campaign costs. Attribution reports do not prove the $800 is incremental; a suitably designed holdout would be needed to investigate that.</p>
        <h2>Migration and email boundaries</h2>
        <p>Archive permission records, suppression lists, active journeys and number-transfer requirements before changing SMS sender. Do not activate equivalent flows in both systems for the same cohort. Postscript has announced email with waitlist links, so verify availability if consolidation is part of the plan. Recart campaign-library references to email are not evidence of an equivalent email sending product.</p>
        <h2>Decision</h2>
        <p>Choose based on the demonstrated signup journey, launch change process and contracted service scope. A merchant with frequent drops needs controlled campaign execution in either system; a recovery-led merchant still needs permissions, suppression and support. No universal revenue-share threshold or outcome winner is established.</p>
        <h2>Where Sequenzy fits</h2>
        <p>Sequenzy lists Shopify customer, order and catalog sync and commerce email automations on its pricing page. Consider it when email is the job you need to replace. Demonstrate required trigger fields, stop conditions and channel handoffs before assuming it can reproduce this page’s exercise. Compare current quotes and implementation work; this page claims no automatic price or outcome advantage.</p>
        <h2>Primary references and limits</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://recart.com/">recart.com</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://postscript.io/pricing">postscript.io/pricing</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://postscript.io/launch">postscript.io/launch</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.sequenzy.com/pricing">www.sequenzy.com/pricing</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p>Vendor pages establish advertised scope, not measured performance, account eligibility or contractual service. Confirm destination support and required features for the selected account. Have the actual messaging permissions and send settings reviewed for the regions you serve; product tooling is not a legal clearance.</p>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-white">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-sendlane">Postscript vs Sendlane</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript">Klaviyo vs Postscript</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-attentive">Postscript vs Attentive</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/beauty">Email apps for beauty stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">SMS cart recovery playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Recart vs Postscript FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
